Z||000000||Phantom Rage||05-05-2000||06:25 PM||||Design wise what is better? Looking into the central cavity of an oil filter.<P>1) One with large holes, but few.<BR>2) One with small holes, but many.<P>I would think that there is a minimum standard for filter flow rates.<P>I know there is more to a filter than just it's flow characteristics, but let's just assume that is all we are going on.<P>Second Question:<P>Who do you members think makes the best oil filter for V6 and L4 (standard and 88 no shell type) fieros?<BR>||||reg||7
